{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, retain existing embeddings and final-real-position readout. Add a residual feed-forward block h'=LayerNorm(h+W2 GELU(W1 h)), with width 2H, after the GRU at every supervised position. Jointly set dropout=0.2, Adam LR=0.0005, weight_decay=0.00001 and batch_size=256. The residual block adds nonlinear compatibility while the lower learning rate and stronger regularization control its added capacity. Preserve history handling, sampling and BPR.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, replace tied embeddings with separate 96-dimensional input and output tables, retaining raw embedding norms. Add a jointly trained gated projection q=sigmoid(Wg h)*tanh(Wq h) for dot-product scoring against output embeddings. Jointly use Adam LR=0.0007, dropout=0.15, weight_decay=0.00001 and batch_size=256. Separate tables decouple recurrent inputs from ranking geometry; the gate and regularization constrain this extra flexibility. Preserve history handling, final-real-position readout, sampling and BPR.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, factor item embeddings into a shared 64-dimensional table and separate learned input/output projections to 128 dimensions. Use two residual GRU blocks. Replace final-state-only readout with a learned gate combining the final real state and attention-pooled observed-prefix states, adding a learned nonnegative recency penalty to attention logits. Training pooling must be causal at every supervised position. Set maxlen=64, dropout=0.2, Adam LR=0.0005 and weight_decay=0.00001. Compact embeddings regularize the deeper recurrence while pooling preserves useful earlier interests. Preserve sampling and BPR.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, retain embedding dimensions and tying, but apply learned per-channel affine LayerNorm only to input embeddings, keeping padding zero and candidate embeddings unnormalized. Replace direct hidden-state scoring with q=h+W2 GELU(W1 h), followed by a learned diagonal bilinear compatibility q^T diag(a)e_item, initialized with a=1. Input normalization stabilizes GRU dynamics while the residual scorer learns channel-specific ranking geometry without removing candidate norms, unlike the previously regressed full L2 normalization. Preserve all training hyperparameters, history handling, final-real-position readout, sampling and BPR."
}
